[{"sha":"6e94a0741348fec9e0cd3ebbfe78cdfa8f818cb6","node_id":"C_kwDOEFLz89oAKDZlOTRhMDc0MTM0OGZlYzllMGNkM2ViYmZlNzhjZGZhOGY4MThjYjY","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/6e94a0741348fec9e0cd3ebbfe78cdfa8f818cb6","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/6e94a0741348fec9e0cd3ebbfe78cdfa8f818cb6","author":{"name":"Ben Munro Wild","email":"ben.munrowild@enactor.co.uk","date":"2026-04-29T10:08:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"Ben Munro Wild","email":"ben.munrowild@enactor.co.uk","date":"2026-04-29T10:08:58Z"},"tree":{"sha":"d015ef770629331cd571c3e858e5b7fbbfe5341c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/trees/d015ef770629331cd571c3e858e5b7fbbfe5341c"},"message":"oidc: handle groups claim as string or array (FlexibleStringSlice)\n\nSome OIDC providers (notably JumpCloud) return the `groups` claim as\na plain string when the user belongs to a single group, rather than\na single-element array:\n\n  Single group:    {\"groups\": \"MyGroup\"}\n  Multiple groups: {\"groups\": [\"Group1\", \"Group2\"]}\n\nThis causes `json.Unmarshal` to fail with:\n\n  cannot unmarshal string into Go struct field OIDCClaims.groups of type []string\n\nThis is the same class of issue as #2293 (FlexibleBoolean for\nemail_verified). The fix follows the same pattern: introduce a\nFlexibleStringSlice type with a custom UnmarshalJSON that accepts\nboth a string and a []string, and use it for the Groups field in\nboth OIDCClaims and OIDCUserInfo.\n\nIncludes test cases for array, single string, and empty array.","parents":[{"sha":"a7d405a25564efe2b09e83a79cd68c31a1ccd6cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/a7d405a25564efe2b09e83a79cd68c31a1ccd6cb","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/a7d405a25564efe2b09e83a79cd68c31a1ccd6cb"}],"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null},"event":"committed"},{"id":24984830384,"node_id":"RRE_lADOEFLz8